    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "",
      "prov:value": "---\nname: sub-kg-lifecycle\ndescription: >-\n  A sub-KG is a knowledge graph staged as a directory inside a harnessed\n  repository, declared as its own instance, that may later leave for a\n  repository of its own. The lifecycle: declare it in place, grow it, stage it\n  for separation (one import seam, the separation guard, a self-contained\n  rehearsal), and then, each behind an explicit owner confirmation, create the\n  repository, copy the staged contents in with history, re-point the\n  declaration, verify on a fresh clone and delete the in-repo copy. Extracted\n  in retrospect from the staged IG separations of 2026-09-21 to 2026-10-06\n  (beans n3ni, rbz3, kg83, hcpz). The light sibling of kg-separation: use this\n  for a DATA instance that leaves whole, and kg-separation when a graph must\n  split into a content repository and a tools repository.\n---",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Sub-KG lifecycle — staged here, separated later",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-06: *\"if user creates it in a folio/, then it can move it to\nanother repo later (this is essentially the create a sub-KG process and skills\nwe have been doing in last week … once the sub KG is staged for separation in\na repo, a new repo is created and staging contents copied into it)\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Sub-KG lifecycle — staged here, separated later",
      "prov:value": "This skill is that week, written down. **Nothing in it was designed first.**\nEvery stage below is a step some session actually took, and each cites where.\nWhere the week did something the hard way, the stage says what to do instead."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The stages",
      "prov:value": "| # | stage | lane | done when | learned from |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | Brief, claim the bean | `authoring-agent` | bean claimed with `bun run cat beans:claim` | [`opening-brief`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/opening-brief.md) |\n| 1 | **Declare it in place** | `authoring-agent` | the declaration parses; `instance-repositories.test.ts` green | bean `6rmv` (identity), `dh4f` (declare only what exists) |\n| 2 | **Grow it in place** | `authoring-agent` | the content type's own gates | the content type's skill |\n| 3 | **Push generic down** | `platform-authoring-agent` | `check:import-direction`, `check:reference-direction`, `check:process-bindings` add nothing | stages A–C of `n3ni` (#1768, #1782, #1783); stage D `kg83` (#1795) |\n| 4 | **One import seam** | `platform-authoring-agent` | every climb out of the directory goes through `<name>/platform.ts` | `6f19f9100` (#1767), `a93da7d41` (#1860) |\n| 5 | **Rehearse self-contained** | `build-pipeline` | `bun run cat seed:ready --layer <name> --rehearse` | `rbz3` (fork rehearsal), `hcpz` (#1896) |\n| 6 | **Report what would move** | `authoring-agent` | the report is in the bean | `kg-separation` stage 9 |\n| 7 | **Owner confirms: create the repository** | `administrator` | an answer, recorded in the bean | separation arc G6 |\n| 8 | Create the repository | `administrator` | it exists, empty, and was read before writing | separation arc G6/G7 |\n| — | `Ready to seed?` | `build-pipeline` | `seed-readiness-gate.dmn` answers `settled` | `hcpz` |\n| 9 | **Copy the staged contents in, with history** | `authoring-agent` | a reviewed PR on a branch of the new repository | `n3ni` stage E, the fork's PR #5 |\n| 10 | **Re-point the declaration** | `platform-authoring-agent` | the host is green consuming the new repository | separation arc G5, S8 |\n| 11 | **Verify on a fresh clone** | `build-pipeline` | the new repository's gates green from `git clone` in an empty directory | #2082, `w1gy` |\n| 12 | **Owner confirms: delete the in-repo copy** | `administrator` | an answer, recorded in the bean | `n3ni` stage F, arc S8 |\n| 13 | Cutover commit | `administrator` | one commit, revertable | `kg-separation` stage 13 |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 6rmv",
        "#1768",
        "#1782",
        "#1783",
        "#1795",
        "#1767",
        "#1860",
        "#1896",
        "#2082"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "1 · Declare it in place",
      "prov:value": "- **`repository` differs from `livesAt.repository`** — that difference is\n  what makes the directory a *staged* instance, and it is what the separation\n  guard and `seed:ready` read. Nothing lists the staged instances by hand.\n- **The directory may sit anywhere** — a root sibling is the precedent (the\n  owner chose a root sibling over a nested folder on 2026-09-21), but the\n  tools read `livesAt.path`, so `folio/<name>/` works the same.\n- **Scaffold it with `init-folio --staged <path>`** (owner ruling 1,\n  2026-10-06):",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21",
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "1 · Declare it in place",
      "prov:value": "  It writes exactly two files, `<path>/<name>.json` and an empty\n  `<path>/platform.ts`, and nothing at the host's root;\n  `init-folio-staged.test.ts` snapshots the whole host tree to hold that.\n  **Never `--instance` inside a host**: it writes a repository's worth of\n  scaffolding (`AGENTS.md`, `.mcp.json`, a beans store, a session hook; 15\n  files, measured with `--dry-run`). `--instance` is for stage 8's repository.\n- **Declare a directory with its files, in one commit** (bean `dh4f`): a\n  declared-but-absent directory is scanned as empty and reported clean.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean dh4f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "3 · Push generic down — before the seam, not after",
      "prov:value": "The week's order was: move everything generic into the harness below\n(stages A–C), consolidate what the sub-KG needs into its own harness\n(stage D), and only then seed. Doing it the other way round copies generic\ncode into a repository that has to give it back."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "3 · Push generic down — before the seam, not after",
      "prov:value": "Wrong-direction edges hide in **declarations and data**, not only in imports.\nThe separation plan found six, and no import check had caught any of them: a\nskill definition naming a package one layer up, a `dependsOn`, a publication\ntarget enumerated in an input schema, prose links, and two `needs` edges to an\nempty layer. So run all three direction checks, not one."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "4 · One import seam: `<name>/platform.ts`",
      "prov:value": "`cat-harness-tools/scripts/tests/instance-separation-imports.test.ts` is the guard.\nIt covers **every** instance whose `repository` differs from its\n`livesAt.repository` — not only those that opted in, because the opt-in\nversion was silent in exactly the case it existed for: the one climb that\nfailed in the fork (`pages-markdown.test.ts`, #2082) sat in an instance with no\nseam. Layers other instances build on are an explicit, checked exemption, and\nan instance that still climbs has a ceiling that may only fall.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2082"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "4 · One import seam: `<name>/platform.ts`",
      "prov:value": "**Create the seam at stage 1, not here.** It costs one file on day one; the\nweek paid 25 reroutes in 10 files for one instance, then 17 more after a\nsingle merge from `main`. A merge is where new climbs arrive, so a red guard\nafter one is the expected signal to reroute, not a regression."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "5 · Rehearse self-contained — run the gates, do not scan",
      "prov:value": "It copies the layer and what it `needs` into a scratch workspace of sibling\ndirectories and runs the tests there. The fork rehearsal (`rbz3`) is why\nthis is a run rather than a reading:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean rbz3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "9 · Copy the staged contents in, with history",
      "prov:value": "The staged directory becomes the new repository's content **with its\nhistory**: `git subtree split --prefix=<name>` in the host, then\n`git subtree add` (or a merge of the split branch) in the new repository.\nThe first fork seed carried 378 commits this way. It goes in on a **branch,\nas a draft PR**, never straight to `main` (separation arc S7). The new\nrepository's own root files — its declaration at the root, its config, its\n`README` — are a second commit in the same PR, so the copy itself stays\nbyte-identical and reviewable."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "10 · Re-point the declaration",
      "prov:value": "| what changes | how |\n|---|---|\n| `livesAt` | removed in the new repository — absent means \"sits at the root of `repository`\" |\n| the seam | `platform.ts` points at wherever the platform now is: a remote-mounted path, or a sibling checkout |\n| the host | **remote mount** if the host imports code from the sub-KG — a `source.remote` instance in the host's root `index.config.json` ([`remote-mount`](../kg-core/remote-mount.md); never a submodule, owner 2026-10-06); **subscription** (`kg:subscribe`) if it only reads its content (separation arc G5) |\n| pins | the host pins a commit while staging, a version once released ([`upstream-version-adoption`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/upstream-version-adoption.md)) |\n| its site | the new repository publishes and previews itself ([`feature-staging`](../../../sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/feature-staging.md), *Which site*): `\"site\": { \"agentRun\": true }` in its `index.config.json` when an agent publishes it, plus whatever workflow its publisher layer's own creation skill requires (an IG's AST-cache refresh, for one) |\n| its checks | `.github/workflows/harness-pr-checks.yml` calling the tools layer's `layer-pr-checks.yml`, so its gates run on every pull request |\n| its QA record | when it declares a `qa` directory with `storage` (`test/results/`, `cat/cat-harness/qa-reports`, keyed by commit): `.github/workflows/publish-qa.yml` calling the tools layer's `layer-qa-publish.yml`, so every push to `main` and every pull request publishes its results to **its own** qa-reports branch, and `test/results/` in `.gitignore`. A host reads them at the commit it pins. Missing from every layer separated before 2026-11-03: the declarations named a store that no job wrote, and once a layer stopped committing its results no reader could find them (bean folio-assistant-7mwa) |\n| `.gitignore` | the mount block, written by the mount tool between its own markers. Never typed: a hand-written marker makes `remote-mount.ts` refuse (*markers unpaired*) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06",
        "2026-11-03"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06",
        "2026-11-03"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "10 · Re-point the declaration",
      "prov:value": "**Copy these from a sibling repository of the same kind; never type them.**\nEvery row above was missing or wrong in a repository scaffolded by hand on\n2026-10-15. Its site could not be built until each was copied in.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "11 · Verify on a fresh clone",
      "prov:value": "The Tool `sub-kg-verify-clone` (owner ruling 2, 2026-10-06) clones the new\nrepository into an empty scratch directory with its submodules (and each\n`--sibling` beside it), installs, and runs its own `gates` script, else its\n`test` script. An empty tree, a failed clone or a repository with no gate is\n`unknown`, never green. **The measured falsifier**\n(#2082): the first seeded fork's test failed with\n`Cannot find module '../../../<harness>/…'`, because nothing in a seed runs\nstandalone until the seam is re-pointed. A rehearsal in the host's scratch\nspace is not this check; it shares the host's `node_modules` and network.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2082",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "11 · Verify on a fresh clone",
      "prov:value": "## What the week did NOT settle"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the week did NOT settle",
      "prov:value": "The owner ruled on three questions on 2026-10-06 (bean `3tza`): *\"1 2 y / 3\nread only mirror in fsh-guts\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 3tza",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "What the week did NOT settle",
      "prov:value": "- **Ruled and built:** `init-folio --staged` (stage 1) and\n  `sub-kg:verify-clone` (stage 11).\n- **Ruled and built: stage 13** (owner, 2026-10-06, \"1\"). After cutover the\n  host keeps a **frozen** copy in [`fsh-guts`](../kg-core/fsh-guts.md), not a\n  refreshed mirror and not a deletion. Step 12 asks (1) move to fsh-guts now,\n  (2) keep in place until the first release, (3) show the file list first,\n  default (2). Step 13 deposits the directory into the PARENT's fsh-guts\n  as a verified archive, then removes it from `main` (owner, 2026-10-06,\n  choosing this archive form over plain trees, which CI then audited as\n  live content). The deposit is the one `state:seed --cutover` makes for a\n  state graph: an archive that must extract to the exact tree being\n  removed, plus a provenance note (`movedFrom`, `movedOn`, `sourceCommit`,\n  `tree`), and the removal commit is made only once it has landed. A\n  separation targets the parent's fsh-guts rather than the departing\n  instance's, which `--cutover` does not do; the separation mode is\n  follow-up work to #2322. The live\n  copy is the remote mount (`index.config.json` `source.remote`), npm package retrieval (`kg-retrieve-npm`), or subscription (`kg:subscribe`) from stage 10; the frozen one is\n  never refreshed and never rendered.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2322",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/kg/graph-management/sub-kg-lifecycle.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "How checks treat a frozen subtree",
      "prov:value": "- **Recognised by declaration, never by path.** A directory is frozen because\n  `<name>.md` beside it declares `$schema: folio-fsh-guts/v1` and\n  `kind: separated-instance` (`isFrozenSubtree` in `schemas/kg/fsh-guts.ts`). A\n  copy dropped in with no note, or under a note of another kind, is walked\n  like any directory, so its files fail self-declaration loudly rather than\n  vanishing from every check.\n- **The note must carry all four stage-13 fields** — `movedFrom`, `movedOn`,\n  `repository`, `matchesCommit` — because it is now the only thing any check\n  reads about thousands of files. Those beyond the common set are exported\n  under the node's `data`.\n- **Materialization records inside are not judged.** They claim bytes in the\n  repository the graph now lives in, which the copy deliberately does not\n  carry.\n- **The note's `bean:` resolves against main's work plan, with no pending\n  escape.** So the deposit lands on the fsh-guts branch in the same step that\n  merges the PR carrying that bean, never before it. The first cutover\n  (2026-10-06, bean `61t6`) was pushed ahead of its PR and turned every PR's\n  CI red until it was held back.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 61t6",
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
